cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "handle-correlation: evidence-ranked same-actor scoring for observed handles"
message: "If you use this software or the method it implements, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Karumudi
    # Add your ORCID before release; it makes the work
    # machine-linkable to you across citation systems.
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
    given-names: Tushar
repository-code: "https://github.com/tusharkarumudi/handle-correlation"
abstract: >-
  A scoring model for deciding whether observed usernames and handles belong to
  the same actor. Recovers handle roots under leetspeak, separator, affix and
  homoglyph mutation; derives evidence weight from measured handle selectivity
  rather than match count; and places all same-root evidence in one correlation
  group so that reuse across N platforms counts as one observation of one naming
  habit rather than N independent confirmations. Performs no enumeration:
  input is observations the analyst has already collected.
keywords:
  - username correlation
  - sockpuppet detection
  - threat actor attribution
  - open source intelligence
  - entity resolution
license: Apache-2.0
version: 2.0.0
